=== Climate ===
Kiso Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate with highland modification (Köppen ''Am''), characterised by warm temperatures, heavy rainfall, and the moderating influence of the mountain terrain. The Kiso Valley, at 400–600 m elevation, experiences slightly cooler temperatures than the coastal lowlands, with more pronounced diurnal variation and frequent morning fog—conditions that are ideal for both ''hinoki'' cypress growth and lacquerware curing.

The Shendan Ocean exposure on the eastern coast brings frequent typhoon impacts and heavy orographic rainfall, with the Kiso Mountains forcing moist air upward and creating rainfall that can exceed 3,800 mm annually in the interior valleys. The forest canopy, however, moderates the rainfall's impact on the ground, and the Kiso Forest's root systems stabilise the mountain slopes against the landslides that plague the more exposed Haruno coast.

